  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Innovative Accountability for Crimes Committed in Syria Since 2011 (2-year Code 3)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SLDP aims to&#xa0;significantly enhance the capacity of Syrian actors and stakeholders to pursue accountability, truth and justice, towards sustainable peace and stability through legal and human rights frameworks.
Programme Strategy:


1.&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0; Dual-track engagement:
&#x25cf;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0; External focus: International advocacy and strategic accountability initiatives.
&#x25cf;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0; Internal focus: Co-building a sustainable human rights culture and supporting victims&apos; rights within Syria.
2.&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0; Core strategic pillars:
&#x25cf;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0; Empowerment of SNGOs, VSFs, WLOS, and grassroot initiatives. 
&#x25cf;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0; Engagement with local duty bearers to support human rights in accordance with international law.
&#x25cf;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0; Corporate accountability for conflict-related human rights violations.
&#x25cf;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0; Human rights due diligence in humanitarian operations.</narrative>
  </description>
